1282
01:01:29.340 --> 01:01:30.080
Kids are fine.

1283
01:01:30.240 --> 01:01:30.740
Jim's fine.

1284
01:01:30.740 --> 01:01:31.240
I'm fine.

1285
01:01:31.380 --> 01:01:31.960
I think we're fine.

1286
01:01:31.980 --> 01:01:33.560
She sort of repeats the word fine.

1287
01:01:33.800 --> 01:01:34.200
Mm-hmm.

1288
01:01:34.200 --> 01:01:40.320
And then Brian was going to say, okay, so things are fine, but are they good?

1289
01:01:40.680 --> 01:01:43.660
And then Pam was going to be like, well, what do you mean?

1290
01:01:43.920 --> 01:01:46.120
And he says, are you happy?

1291
01:01:46.440 --> 01:01:47.040
Mm-hmm.

1292
01:01:47.360 --> 01:01:53.800
And then it was scripted that he was going to brush some of her hair away from her face

1293
01:01:54.600 --> 01:02:01.840
and say that maybe it's not his place to say it, but he thinks she deserves better, that

1294
01:02:01.840 --> 01:02:06.640
she's an amazing woman, and she should be with someone who tells her how amazing she

1295
01:02:06.640 --> 01:02:07.780
is all the time.

1296
01:02:08.440 --> 01:02:13.720
And then Pam was going to get really angry and say, never call me again.

1297
01:02:14.840 --> 01:02:17.000
Well, how do you think that went down?

1298
01:02:17.860 --> 01:02:20.000
Not great, because it was only in the table read.

1299
01:02:20.240 --> 01:02:23.060
I did not reread the table read for this.

1300
01:02:23.140 --> 01:02:25.340
I just read the shooting draft and candy bag alts.

